In .NET 10, `WindowSoftInputModeAdjust.Resize` is obsolete because Android deprecated `adjustResize` itself. The recommended replacement is **`KeyboardAutoManagerScroll`**, which is enabled by default in MAUI and automatically scrolls/pads content when the keyboard opens.

**If it's not working for your chat layout, check these things:**

### 1. Don't disable it accidentally
```csharp
// Do NOT do this:
KeyboardAutoManagerScroll.Disconnect();
```

### 2. Structure your layout so the input is inside a scrollable context or at the bottom of a `Grid`:
```xml
<Grid RowDefinitions="*, Auto">
    <CollectionView Grid.Row="0" ItemsSource="{Binding Messages}" />
    <HorizontalStackLayout Grid.Row="1" Padding="8">
        <Entry Placeholder="Type a message..." HorizontalOptions="FillAndExpand" />
        <Button Text="Send" />
    </HorizontalStackLayout>
</Grid>
```

### 3. If auto-scroll still doesn't work (common with complex layouts), manually adjust on Android using insets:

In `Platforms/Android/MainActivity.cs`:
```csharp
using AndroidX.Core.View;
using Microsoft.Maui.Platform;

protected override void OnCreate(Bundle? savedInstanceState)
{
    base.OnCreate(savedInstanceState);

    ViewCompat.SetOnApplyWindowInsetsListener(Window!.DecorView, new InsetsListener());
}

private class InsetsListener : Java.Lang.Object, IOnApplyWindowInsetsListener
{
    public WindowInsetsCompat OnApplyWindowInsets(Android.Views.View v, WindowInsetsCompat insets)
    {
        var imeInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.Ime());
        var navInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.NavigationBars());

        // Apply bottom padding = keyboard height minus nav bar
        var bottom = Math.Max(imeInsets.Bottom - navInsets.Bottom, 0);
        v.SetPadding(0, 0, 0, bottom);

        return insets;
    }
}
```

### Summary

| Approach | When to use |
|----------|-------------|
| `KeyboardAutoManagerScroll` (default) | Simple layouts — just works |
| Insets listener (above) | Complex/chat layouts where auto-scroll fails |
| `android:windowSoftInputMode="adjustResize"` in manifest | Last resort; still works at OS level but deprecated |

The insets listener approach is the most robust for chat UIs and is the "edge-to-edge" pattern Google now recommends.
